# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Secrets — THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Webhook URLs / tokens / keys live OUTSIDE the
# repo (env vars / ~/.claude). These patterns are a backstop, NOT the plan:
# the plan is to never write a secret into a repo file in the first place.
.env
.env.*
*.local
*secret*
*webhook*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output
.playwright-mcp/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
market-history/layers/tax/*.xls
market-history/layers/appreciation/zhvi_zip.csv
market-history/layers/appreciation/hpi_at_zip5.xlsx
market-history/layers/income/*.dat
market-history/layers/education/*.dat

# Appraiser verdicts: contain a real address, condition commentary on someone else's
# home, and the maximum we would pay for it. See offer/SPIKE-appraiser.md section 12.
# Only the de-identified rows in appraise/appraisal-grades/ are ever committed.
market-history/appraise/appraisals/
market-history/appraise/run/

# Screenshots dropped at the repo root while working on a design (trifecta-*.png,
# mobile-*.png, final-desktop.png, four-towns.png and friends). Nothing in the repo
# references them, they run ~400 KB each, and git history is forever on a public
# repo — so they stay local. A screenshot that IS documentation belongs next to the
# thing it documents, committed deliberately, not loose in the root.
/*.png

# Experiments — scratch analyses that are NOT routines. Kept on disk so agents
# can read and re-run them, deliberately never committed: they are one-off
# explorations, they carry big fetched caches (a few MB of Scryfall JSON), and
# a public repo does not need them in history forever. If an experiment ever
# graduates into something real, it moves out of here and gets committed on
# purpose.
/experiments/
